{#- Article cards (REQ-013, REQ-016): the newest-first `posts` collection as
    .post cards — the article's image (si-awlu), date, the category chip (a
    link to the category page), the draft chip when the article is a draft,
    the title link and the description. Set `posts` before including; set
    `listHeading` to "h3" when the list sits under an h2 (default "h2"). The
    image is the article's WebP copies (scripts/lib/images.mjs) with alt="",
    as the title link beside it names the article: below 48rem, on a phone,
    the 600 px copy, and from 48rem the copy the card's width asks for. It
    loads lazily unless its card is one of the first `eagerCards` (default
    none): the blog index and the category pages set 2, the first row, which
    may be on the first screen, and those load at once but after the
    stylesheets and fonts (fetchpriority="low"), as the text of the first
    screen comes before its pictures. The empty state is blog.empty. -#}
{%- set headingTag = listHeading or "h2" -%}
{%- set eager = eagerCards or 0 -%}
{%- if posts | length %}
  <ol class="post-list">
    {%- for post in posts %}
    {%- set img = post.data.image | articleImage(post.page.fileSlug) %}
    <li class="post reveal">
      <picture>
        <source media="(max-width: 47.99rem)" srcset="{{ img.small }}">
        <img class="post-image" src="{{ img.src }}" srcset="{{ img.srcset }}" sizes="35rem" width="{{ shareImage.width }}" height="{{ shareImage.height }}" alt=""{% if loop.index > eager %} loading="lazy"{% else %} fetchpriority="low"{% endif %}>
      </picture>
      <p class="post-meta">
        <time datetime="{{ post.date | isoDate }}">{{ post.date | localeDate(lang) }}</time>
        <a class="chip chip-cat" href="{{ langPrefix }}/blog/{{ post.data.category }}/">{{ strings[lang].categories[post.data.category] }}</a>
        {%- if post.data.draft %}
        <span class="chip chip-draft"><span class="chip-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ strings[lang].article.draftLabel }}</span>
        {%- endif %}
      </p>
      <{{ headingTag }} class="post-title"><a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }}</a></{{ headingTag }}>
      <p class="post-text">{{ post.data.description }}</p>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ol>
{%- else %}
  <p class="post-empty">{{ strings[lang].blog.empty }}</p>
{%- endif %}
